"OPPOSITION Definition & Meaning - Merriam-Webster (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/opposition)\nciteturn39view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/opposition\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 233\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】 【1†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search Dictionary]\nL3: \nL4:   * 【2†Games】\nL5:   * 【3†Word of the Day】\nL6:   * 【4†Grammar】\nL7:   * 【5†Word Finder】\nL8:   * 【6†Slang】\nL9:   * 【7†Newsletters】\nL10:   * 【8†Wordplay】\nL11:   * 【9†Rhymes】\nL12:   * 【10†Thesaurus】\nL13:   * 【11†Join MWU†unabridged.merriam-webster.com】\nL14:   * More\nL15:     * 【2†Games】\nL16:     * 【3†Word of the Day】\nL17:     * 【4†Grammar】\nL18:     * 【8†Wordplay】\nL19:     * 【6†Slang】\nL20:     * 【9†Rhymes】\nL21:     * 【5†Word Finder】\nL22:     * 【7†Newsletters】\nL23:     * 【10†Thesaurus】\nL24:     * 【11†Join MWU†unabridged.merriam-webster.com】\nL25:     * Shop\nL26:     * 【12†Books†shop.merriam-webster.com】\nL27:     * 【13†Merch†merriamwebster.threadless.com】\nL28: \nL29: 【14†Dictionary】\nL30: \nL31:   * # opposition\nL32: ## 【15†noun】\nL33: \nL34: op·​po·​si·​tion 【16†ˌä-pə-ˈzi-shən 】\nL35: \nL36: 【17†Synonyms of opposition】\nL37: \nL38: Simple Definition A Simple Definition is available from our Learner's Dictionary to help you understand the meaning faster.\nL39: \nL40: 1\nL41: \nL42: : an act of setting opposite or over against : the condition of being so set\nL43: \nL44: He spoke in opposition to the new law.\nL45: \nL46: 2\nL47: \nL48: : hostile or contrary action or condition\nL49: \nL50: offered strong opposition to the advance of the enemy\nL51: \nL52: 3\nL53: \nL54: a\nL55: \nL56: : something that opposes\nL57: specifically : a body of persons opposing something\nL58: \nL59: Each candidate is focused on raising more money than the opposition.\nL60: \nL61: b\nL62: \nL63: often Opposition : a political party opposing and prepared to replace the party in power\nL64: \nL65: The opposition is likely to win the upcoming election.\nL66: \nL67: 4\nL68: : a configuration (see 【18†configuration sense 1b】) in which one celestial (see 【19†celestial entry 1 sense 2】) body is opposite another (such as the sun) in the sky or in which the elongation (see 【20†elongation sense 1】) is near or equal to 180 degrees\nL69: \nL70: 5\nL71: \nL72: logic : the relation between two 【21†propositions】 having the same subject and predicate but differing in quantity or quality or both\nL73: \nL74: The propositions \"Every box is empty\" and \"Some box is not empty\" are in contradictory opposition.\nL75: \nL76: oppositional\nL77: 【22†ˌä-pə-ˈzi-sh(ə-)nəl 】\nL78: \nL79: adjective\nL80: ## Synonyms of opposition\nL81: \nL82: Relevance\nL83: \nL84:   * 【23†resistance】\nL85:   * 【24†objection】\nL86: \nL87: 【17†See All Synonyms & Antonyms in Thesaurus】\nL88: ## Examples of opposition in a Sentence\nL89: They're going ahead with the plans despite strong opposition from residents. The nominee faces strong opposition in the Senate. The proposed change has met with opposition from the town's business leaders. Rebels have so far offered little opposition to advancing troops. Each candidate is focused on raising more money than the opposition. The coach advised her team not to underestimate the opposition. The leader of the Opposition criticized the prime minister for his comments. See More\nL90: Recent Examples on the Web\nL91: \nL92: Examples are automatically compiled from online sources to show current usage. 【14†Read More】 Opinions expressed in the examples do not represent those of Merriam-Webster or its editors. 【25†Send us feedback†docs.google.com】.\nL93: Sidelined opposition Washington has so far sidelined Machado from the political transition process despite having a friendly relationship with the opposition leader. — Michael Rios, CNN Money, 29 Oct. 2026 Fortune has reported that Gen Z has become an organizing force behind the national backlash, and that opposition has spread well beyond the small share of Americans who actually live near a data center. — Sasha Tuddenham, Fortune, 29 Oct.\nL94: 2026 This was a rather diplomatic answer from a man whose company once ran advertisements welcoming refugees in pointed opposition to Trump’s 2017 Muslim travel ban. — Maxwell Adler, Vanity Fair, 29 Oct. 2026 Any tax redistribution plan next year will face opposition from the governor. — Keith M. Phaneuf, Hartford Courant, 29 Oct. 2026 【26†See All Example Sentences for opposition】\nL95: ## Word History\nL96: \nL97: Etymology\nL98: Middle English opposicioun \"location opposite something, contrary opinion, opposition of celestial bodies,\" borrowed from Middle French & Latin; Middle French oposicion (Anglo-French opposicion \"objection, questioning\"), borrowed from Medieval Latin oppositiōn-, oppositiō, going back to Late Latin, \"contradiction, antithesis\" (loan translation of Greek antíthesis), from Latin opposi-, variant stem of oppōnere \"to place (over or against), place as an obstacle, set in opposition to, argue in reply\" + -tiōn-, -tiō, suffix of verbal action — more at 【27†oppose】\nL99: First Known Use\nL100: \nL101: 14th century, in the meaning defined at 【28†sense 1】\nL102: \nL103: Time Traveler\nL104: \nL105: The first known use of opposition was in the 14th century\nL106: \nL107: 【29†See more words from the same century】\nL108: ## Browse Nearby Words\nL109: \nL110: 【30†oppositi-】\nL111: \nL112: opposition\nL113: \nL114: 【31†oppositional】\nL115: \nL116: 【32†See all Nearby Words】\nL117: \nL118: ## Cite this Entry\nL119: \nL120: Style\nL121: \nL122: [Select]\nL123: \nL124: “Opposition.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/opposition. Accessed 1 Nov. 2026.\nL125: \nL126: 【33†Image†prod.cdn-mw.com】Copy Citation\nL127: ## Kids Definition\nL128: \nL129: opposition\nL130: \nL131: noun\nL132: \nL133: op·​po·​si·​tion 【16†ˌäp-ə-ˈzish-ən 】\nL134: \nL135: 1\nL136: \nL137: : the state of being opposite\nL138: \nL139: 2\nL140: \nL141: : the action of resisting\nL142: \nL143: offer opposition to a plan\nL144: \nL145: the opposition of two forces\nL146: \nL147: 3\nL148: \nL149: a\nL150: \nL151: : a group of persons (as a team or an enemy force) that oppose someone or something\nL152: \nL153: b\nL154: \nL155: often capitalized : a political party opposing the party in power\nL156: ## More from Merriam-Webster on opposition\nL157: \nL158: Britannica.com: 【34†Encyclopedia article about opposition†www.britannica.com】\nL159: \nL160: Love words? Need even more definitions?\nL161: \nL162: Subscribe to America's largest dictionary and get thousands more definitions and advanced search—ad free!\nL163: \nL164: Last Updated: 30 Oct 2026 - Updated example sentences\nL165: \nL166: ## More from Merriam-Webster\nL167: \nL168: #### 【3†Word of the Day】\nL169: \nL170: #### 【3†Pyrrhic】\nL171: \nL172: 【3†See Definitions and Examples】 »\nL173: ## Popular in Grammar & Usage\nL174: \nL175: 【4†See More】\nL176: \nL177: 【35†How to Use 'Who' vs. 'Whom'】\nL178: \nL179: 【36†Merriam-Webster’s Great Big List of Words You Love to Hate】\nL180: \nL181: 【37†'Affect' vs. 'Effect'】\nL182: \nL183: 【38†'A' or 'an'? What about before 'h'? An Indefinite Article Guide】\nL184: \nL185: 【39†Why is '-ed' sometimes pronounced at the end of a word?】\nL186: ## Popular in Wordplay\nL187: \nL188: 【8†See More】\nL189: \nL190: 【40†The Longest Long Words List】\nL191: \nL192: 【41†9 Words That Sound Like Insults But Aren't】\nL193: \nL194: 【42†Pwn, Skibidi, Girlboss and Other Words Added to the 2026 Scrabble Dictionary】\nL195: \nL196: 【43†The Words of the Week - Oct. 30】\nL197: \nL198: 【44†12 Lovely and Unusual Words for the Natural World】\nL199: \nL200: ## Popular\nL201: \nL202: 【8†See More】\nL203: \nL204: 【35†How to Use 'Who' vs. 'Whom'】\nL205: \nL206: 【40†The Longest Long Words List】\nL207: \nL208: 【41†9 Words That Sound Like Insults But Aren't】\n